    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "5f15ee11-19f8-301c-a845-871e15dc09fc",
                "word": "masculinism",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "7db4a389-f62c-470f-be95-52b911fb152c",
                        "entry_id": "5f15ee11-19f8-301c-a845-871e15dc09fc",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "masculinisms"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "85f7eb8b-fceb-3455-ba56-c89d08b9fbc3",
                        "entry_id": "5f15ee11-19f8-301c-a845-871e15dc09fc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An ideology of masculinity or of male rights; considered as opposed to feminism."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "28f75ac1-1e1c-4766-b447-d91b3fc5cc01",
                                "sense_id": "85f7eb8b-fceb-3455-ba56-c89d08b9fbc3",
                                "text": "While only women can participate in the building of a feminist culture, without the interference — however well-intentioned — of men, men can facilitate that process by refusing to participate in the old order of masculinism."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd775152-fb9f-4534-b65b-d64807bd987a",
                                "sense_id": "85f7eb8b-fceb-3455-ba56-c89d08b9fbc3",
                                "text": "[…] the transition to liberal capitalism offers men the opportunity of putting a greatly increased social distance between themselves and women. It is the rise of masculinism which is the primary characteristic of gender relations in Eastern Europe today."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2009b6a8-d8f1-4ec6-8b36-9dee03043129",
                                "sense_id": "85f7eb8b-fceb-3455-ba56-c89d08b9fbc3",
                                "text": "[…] a lonely straight male had no equivalently forgiving Theory of Masculinism to help him out of this bind, this key to all misogynies: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "999940a5-019b-4eca-8f3d-13cc3cf4df44",
                                "sense_id": "85f7eb8b-fceb-3455-ba56-c89d08b9fbc3",
                                "text": "Each is laden with assumptions and appropriations that, in discursive terms, reinforce a culture of masculinism – the cultural dominance of the male (in the public sphere)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c656b8f4-c369-41a1-a9fc-35eb0d2b74c6",
                                "sense_id": "85f7eb8b-fceb-3455-ba56-c89d08b9fbc3",
                                "text": "However, it is possible to examine the broader historical contours of masculinism – the ideology that justifies male domination – and the masculinist institutions that endorse masculinism […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e7476b52-2d70-3406-a8e2-da364ab8db38",
                        "entry_id": "5f15ee11-19f8-301c-a845-871e15dc09fc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Mannishness."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "994b6d1e-a169-411a-9f58-4737d4d1be9d",
                                "sense_id": "e7476b52-2d70-3406-a8e2-da364ab8db38",
                                "text": "The greater part of these various anatomical peculiarities and functional anomalies point, more or less clearly, to the prevalence among inverts of a tendency to infantilism, combined with feminism in men and masculinism in women"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
